# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": any line may use any name the block binds; the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else), ch. 8 (`<-` builds the child and binds its result; a widget application is transparent) and ruling TC (places counted as built: the loud arm builds place 1, so the widget's own label is 2 and the last label 3; the soft arm builds none, so they are 1 and 2). Never run: prismc refuses the program.
